# Install

Download both apps from the [latest release](https://github.com/kykurniawan/ligarview/releases/latest):

- `Ligarview-<version>-macos-arm64.dmg` for the Mac (Apple Silicon, macOS 14 or newer)
- `Ligarview-<version>.apk` for the Android tablet (Android 11 or newer)

The builds are not signed with an Apple Developer ID and are not notarized, and the APK is signed with the project's own key rather than distributed through Google Play. Both therefore show a one-time warning, described below. `SHA256SUMS` in the release lets you check your downloads.

## The Mac app

1. Open the `.dmg` and drag **Ligarview** into **Applications**.
2. Open it. macOS says it cannot verify the app. Open **System Settings → Privacy & Security**, scroll to **Security** and press **Open Anyway** next to Ligarview, then confirm. Or remove the quarantine flag once from a terminal:

   ```bash
   xattr -dr com.apple.quarantine /Applications/Ligarview.app
   ```

3. Allow **Screen Recording** when asked, in **System Settings → Privacy & Security → Screen & System Audio Recording**, then open the app again.

## The Android app

1. Download the `.apk` on the tablet, or copy it over and open it from the Files app.
2. Android asks to let that app (your browser or Files) install unknown apps. Allow it for this install.
3. If Play Protect warns about an unrecognized app, choose **More details → Install anyway**.

No USB debugging or developer mode is needed, then or later. To update, install the newer `.apk` over the old one.

<p class="note">Next: <a href="/docs/connect">connect the tablet</a>.</p>

## Build from source

For development. Clone the repository first:

```bash
git clone https://github.com/kykurniawan/ligarview.git
cd ligarview
```

**Mac app.** Needs [Rust](https://rustup.rs) (stable) and Xcode's command line tools. `tools/bundle.sh` builds `host/target/Ligarview.app`; `tools/dmg.sh` also produces the disk image in `dist/`. You can also run the host straight from a terminal, without the window:

```bash
cd host
cargo run --release
```

**Android app.** Needs the Android SDK and JDK 17 or newer. `tools/apk.sh` builds `dist/Ligarview-<version>.apk`, signed with the debug key unless the `LIGARVIEW_KEYSTORE*` variables point at a release key. To install straight onto a tablet with USB debugging on, run `./gradlew installDebug` in `android/`.
